  About intrinsics: Yes, I like the idea of different classes having
class-specific intrinsics, and I would like to have this extended. Without
those every character looks essentially the same once he reaches level
15 or so, independently of what class did he start.
  What I'd love to see is some system of weapon skills, so that each character
class has some weapon they are paricuraly skilled with (and for which they
get plusses when using them) and weapons they are particularly bad at
(so that they get minus to hit, and occasionally fumble). This will 
differentiate classes somewhat more and could make certain weapons
more attractive (should I, as a rogue, use that unwieldy sword or stay
with that dagger they taught me to how to use?)
